 on the monitor.", "viewing tool"], ["모니터가 너무 밝아요.", "The monitor is too bright.", "brightness"], ["큰 모니터를 사고 싶어요.", "I want to buy a big monitor.", "wanting item"]], "nuance": "Refers to a computer display screen, distinct from a TV, which Koreans call 텔레비전 instead.", "mistakes": ["Do not call a TV a 모니터."]}, {"kind": "noun", "hangul": "프린터", "english": "printer", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": ["grammar-particle-ro-euro"], "usage": [["프린터로 인쇄해요.", "I print with the printer.", "tool with euro particle"], ["프린터가 느려요.", "The printer is slow.", "describing speed"], ["프린터를 써요.", "I use the printer.", "using device"], ["프린터가 멈췄어요.", "The printer stopped.", "device stopped"]], "examples": [["프린터로 사진을 뽑아요.", "I print photos with the printer.", "printing photos"], ["회사에 프린터가 있어요.", "There is a printer at work.", "location"], ["프린터에 종이가 없어요.", "The printer has no paper.", "out of paper"]], "nuance": "The machine that prints documents, while the act of printing itself is the verb 인쇄하다 in Korean.", "mistakes": ["Do not mix up 프린터 with 인쇄."]}, {"kind": "noun", "hangul": "스피커", "english": "speaker", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": ["grammar-particle-ro-euro"], "usage": [["스피커로 음악을 들어요.", "I listen to music on the speaker.", "tool with euro particle"], ["스피커가 좋아요.", "The speaker is good.", "describing quality"], ["스피커를 켜요.", "I turn on the speaker.", "turning on"], ["스피커가 작아요.", "The speaker is small.", "describing size"]], "examples": [["스피커로 노래를 틀어요.", "I play songs on the speaker.", "playing songs"], ["스피커 소리가 커요.", "The speaker sound is loud.", "loud sound"], ["새 스피커를 샀어요.", "I bought a new speaker.", "buying item"]], "nuance": "Means the audio device for playing sound, not a person who speaks at an event in Korean usage.", "mistakes": ["Do not use 스피커 for a presenter."]}, {"kind": "noun", "hangul": "이어폰", "english": "earphones", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": ["grammar-particle-ro-euro"], "usage": [["이어폰으로 음악을 들어요.", "I listen to music with earphones.", "tool with euro particle"], ["이어폰이 좋아요.", "The earphones are good.", "describing quality"], ["이어폰을 껴요.", "I put in the earphones.", "wearing earphones"], ["이어폰이 없어요.", "I do not have earphones.", "not having"]], "examples": [["이어폰으로 영어를 공부해요.", "I study English with earphones.", "studying tool"], ["이어폰 줄이 엉켰어요.", "The earphone cord is tangled.", "tangled cord"], ["지하철에서 이어폰을 써요.", "I use earphones on the subway.", "subway use"]], "nuance": "Refers to small in-ear listening devices, while larger over-ear ones are called 헤드폰 in Korean.", "mistakes": ["Do not say 이어폰 for headphones."]}, {"kind": "noun", "hangul": "데이터", "english": "data", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": ["grammar-particle-ro-euro"], "usage": [["데이터로 영상을 봐요.", "I watch videos using data.", "means with euro particle"], ["데이터가 많아요.", "I have a lot of data.", "describing amount"], ["데이터를 다 썼어요.", "I used up all my data.", "using up data"], ["데이터가 느려요.", "The data is slow.", "slow speed"]], "examples": [["데이터로 길을 찾아요.", "I find the way using data.", "navigation use"], ["이번 달 데이터가 부족해요.", "I am short on data this month.", "running low"], ["와이파이가 없어서 데이터를 써요.", "I use data because there is no wifi.", "no wifi"]], "nuance": "In daily life this usually means mobile phone data allowance, not abstract information in research contexts.", "mistakes": ["Do not confuse phone data with 정보."]}, {"kind": "noun", "hangul": "요금제", "english": "phone plan", "topic": "daily-life", "chapterIds": ["chapter-05"], "grammarIds": ["grammar-particle-ro-euro"], "usage": [["새 요금제로 바꿨어요.", "I changed to a new plan.", "change with euro particle"], ["요금제가 비싸요.", "The plan is expensive.", "describing price"], ["요금제를 골라요.", "I choose a plan.", "choosing plan"], ["요금제가 좋아요.", "The plan is good.", "describing quality"]], "examples": [["싼 요금제로 바꾸고 싶어요.", "I want to switch to a cheap plan.", "wanting change"], ["이 요금제는 데이터